  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>trametinib</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>L01EE01</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>two compartments, IV dosing <small>(PK_2C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Ravix A et al. 2024</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>adult oncology patients with solid tumours</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>trametinib</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_trametinib/Trametinib_Ravix2024_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>CL</td><td>4.2</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>central volume (V2)</td><td>102</td><td>L</td><td><small>V1</small></td></tr><tr><td>intercompartmental clearance (Q)</td><td>35.1</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>Q</small></td></tr><tr><td>peripheral volume (V3)</td><td>338</td><td>L</td><td><small>V2</small></td></tr></table><h4>About trametinib</h4><p>Trametinib is a MEK inhibitor anticancer drug used to treat melanoma, including metastatic melanoma, and also studied for other cancers such as non-small-cell lung carcinoma and low-grade serous carcinoma. It is authorised in the European Union, where it is used for melanoma and glioma.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q7833138\">Wikidata Q7833138</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Trametinib\">Trametinib</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Ravix A et al. (2024). Population Pharmacokinetics of Trametinib and Impact of Nonadherence on Drug Exposure in Oncology Patients as Part of the Optimizing Oral Targeted Anticancer Therapies Study. <i>Cancers 16(12)</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers16122193\">10.3390/cancers16122193</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38927898\">38927898</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Ravix_2024: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
